   "subject": "Plotting based on multiple factors/variables",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi, I&#39;m trying to make a readable plot from a data set containing many conditions and am struggling to find a solution.<div><br></div><div>Basically I want to plot nuclear intensity (p65) as it relates to strain (RH, PRU, ME49), broken down by infection level (moi: 1, 5, 10, 20) and status (infected / uninfected).</div><div><br></div><div>I&#39;ve attached shots of my data and code, and the plot that I have so far. The plot is close to what I want, but instead of having status overplotted, I would really like to separate them and have them plotted side by side so it is more apparent how they reflect p65 intensity.</div><div><br></div><div>Cheers!</div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "KVAJdHuTAgAJ",
   "from": "Roman Luštrik",
   "author": "bfc2eb6b71169017",
   "date": "2017-05-03T13:59:04Z",
   "subject": "Re: Plotting based on multiple factors/variables",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms,sans-serif\">One solution would be to create a new variable which is a combination of status and moi. Map that to x axis and you&#39;re done. Something along the lines of</div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms,sans-serif\"><br></div><blockquote style=\"margin:0 0 0 40px;border:none;padding:0px\"><div class=\"gmail_default\"><font face=\"monospace, monospace\">raw.data$moi.status &lt;- with(raw.data, paste(moi, status, sep = &quot;_&quot;))</font></div></blockquote><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms,sans-serif\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms,sans-serif\">and then</div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms,sans-serif\"><br></div><blockquote style=\"margin:0 0 0 40px;border:none;padding:0px\"><div class=\"gmail_default\"><font face=\"monospace, monospace\">ggplot(..., aes(x = moi.status, ...)) + ...</font></div></blockquote><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:&quot;trebuchet ms&quot;,sans-serif\">​Cheers,</div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:&quot;trebuchet ms&quot;,sans-serif\">Roman​</div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Wed, May 3, 2017 at 3:26 PM, Aric Schultz <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">rockc...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br></div></div></div>"
    ],
